FIX / binary protocol over TCP (not REST):
NewOrderSingle   { clOrdId, symbol, side, qty, price, type: LIMIT|MARKET, tif: DAY|IOC|FOK }
OrderCancelRequest { origClOrdId }
ExecutionReport  { orderId, execType: NEW|PARTIAL_FILL|FILL|CANCELED|REJECTED, lastQty, lastPx }
Market data: multicast UDP feed of book deltas + trades, with sequence numbers

def on_limit_buy(o):
    while o.qty and asks.best() and asks.best().price <= o.price:
        lvl = asks.best()
        resting = lvl.queue[0]                 # time priority
        q = min(o.qty, resting.qty)
        emit_trade(o, resting, q, lvl.price)   # trade at resting price
        o.qty -= q; resting.qty -= q
        if resting.qty == 0: lvl.queue.popleft(); index.pop(resting.id)
        if not lvl.queue: asks.remove(lvl)
    if o.qty and o.tif == 'DAY': bids.add(o)   # rest the remainder
